ctok-go is an unofficial, unaffiliated count reconstruction for Claude text.
It is not endorsed by Anthropic and is not an official tokenizer.

The count reconstruction and vocabulary are derived from ctok v1.3.0:
https://github.com/sanderland/ctok
Copyright (c) 2026 Sander Land, MIT License (see LICENSE).
Go implementation contributions: Copyright (c) 2026 Luis Pabon.

No separately licensed upstream evaluation corpora are included.
Unicode classification, case and normalization data reproduce the recorded oracle.
Vendored x/text normalization code uses the BSD license in internal/norm/LICENSE;
its patent grant is retained in internal/norm/PATENTS.
Unicode data notices are retained in UNICODE-LICENSE.
See REFERENCE.json and PROVENANCE.md for source pins and limitations.
